  "name": "mina3",
  "description": "Mina is a layer-1 blockchain protocol utilizing recursive zero-knowledge proofs to maintain a constant-sized state of approximately 22KB. The repository contains the core OCaml implementation of the protocol, Rust-based cryptographic stubs for the Kimchi proof system, and a suite of infrastructure tools for network orchestration, archive nodes, and Rosetta API integration. It supports programmable smart contracts called zkApps, which leverage succinct proofs to ensure privacy and scalability.",
